tags: device-id

A fact of a device: a stable id that the node selects for the device. A caller uses it
to ask for this device (the setting device-selection of Configuration.policies).

The value is 1 to 64 bytes of printable ASCII, with no space, no comma and no "=".
Example: gpu-0. The id is unique among the devices of the node, and it stays the same
when the node restarts.

An absent fact: the node gives no stable id, and a caller cannot select the device.
The node is bound: it attests the fact.

=== formal
class=fact
name=device-id
place=ArchitectureResources.facts
value=1 to 64 bytes, each with a value from 33 to 126, and none with the value 44 (',') or 61 ('='); unique among the devices of the node; the same after a restart of the node
